### Travel Request Service — coleção de requests
# HTTP Client do PhpStorm/IntelliJ: rode de cima para baixo. Os scripts guardam tokens, ids e ETag.
# Precisa de `make up` e `make seed` (contas admin@, luffy@ e zoro@example.com, senha password123).
# Porta diferente de 8000? Troque @host abaixo.

@host = http://localhost:8000
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### 1. Login do solicitante (Luffy)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"email": "luffy@example.com", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("luffy", response.body.access_token);
    client.global.set("luffy_refresh", response.body.refresh_token);
%}

### 2. Login do admin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"email": "admin@example.com", "password": "password123"}

> {% client.global.set("admin", response.body.access_token); %}

### 3. Login do Zoro (outro solicitante)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"email": "zoro@example.com", "password": "password123"}

> {% client.global.set("zoro", response.body.access_token); %}

### 4. Quem sou eu
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Refresh rotativo: o refresh antigo deixa de valer
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"refresh_token": "{{luffy_refresh}}"}

> {%
    client.global.set("luffy", response.body.access_token);
    client.global.set("luffy_refresh", response.body.refresh_token);
%}

### 6. Criar um pedido (201, ETag "1"); o solicitante vem do token
POST {{api}}/travel-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"destination": "Wano", "departure_date": "2027-01-10", "return_date": "2027-01-15"}

> {%
    client.global.set("travel_request", response.body.data.id);
    client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag"));
%}

### 7. Consultar o pedido
GET {{api}}/travel-requests/{{travel_request}}
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Listar com filtros: status, destino, período de criação e de viagem, cursor
GET {{api}}/travel-requests?status=requested&destination=Wano&travel_from=2027-01-01&travel_to=2027-01-31&per_page=10
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Editar o destino (só o dono, só em requested) com If-Match
PATCH {{api}}/travel-requests/{{travel_request}}
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"destination": "Dressrosa"}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### 10. Outro usuário não enxerga o pedido: 404
GET {{api}}/travel-requests/{{travel_request}}
Authorization: Bearer {{zoro}}
Accept: application/json

### 11. Solicitante não decide: 403
POST {{api}}/travel-requests/{{travel_request}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Accept: application/json

### 12. Decisão sem If-Match: 428
POST {{api}}/travel-requests/{{travel_request}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Accept: application/json

### 13. Admin aprova (200, ETag "3"); a notificação chega ao Luffy por banco, e-mail e WebSocket
POST {{api}}/travel-requests/{{travel_request}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Accept: application/json

### 14. Repetir com o ETag antigo: 412 /problems/version-mismatch
POST {{api}}/travel-requests/{{travel_request}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Accept: application/json

### 15. Cancelar um pedido aprovado: 409 /problems/invalid-status-transition
POST {{api}}/travel-requests/{{travel_request}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
If-Match: "3"
Accept: application/json

### 16. Validação: 422 /problems/validation-failed
POST {{api}}/travel-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"destination": "W", "departure_date": "2020-01-01", "return_date": "2019-12-31"}

### 17. Admin vê todos os pedidos
GET {{api}}/travel-requests?per_page=5
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Accept: application/json

### 18. Notificações do Luffy (a mais nova primeiro); unread=true filtra as não lidas
GET {{api}}/notifications?unread=true&per_page=5
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Accept: application/json

> {%
    if (response.body.data.length > 0) {
        client.global.set("notification", response.body.data[0].id);
    }
%}

### 19. Marcar como lida (idempotente)
POST {{api}}/notifications/{{notification}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Accept: application/json

### 20. Logout (204): revoga o access token (lista no Redis) e a família do refresh token
POST {{api}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"refresh_token": "{{luffy_refresh}}"}

### 21. O token revogado não vale mais: 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{luffy}}
Accept: application/json

### 22. Chaves públicas do JWT (JWKS)
GET {{host}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### 23. Saúde: liveness e readiness (MySQL, réplica, Redis, RabbitMQ)
GET {{host}}/health/ready
